  <title>6.2.5: Multiplying Polynomial Functions</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01587</md:content-id>
    <md:title>6.2.5: Multiplying Polynomial Functions</md:title>
    <md:uuid>e63d735c-055b-4154-bc84-18ddd3e87c1e</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><title>Cool Down (5 minutes)</title>
<title>Student Activity</title>
<para>For 1 - 4, use the following polynomial function to complete the multiplication. Use the "^" symbol to enter an exponent.</para>
<blockquote>
\(f(x) = 3x + 2b\)
  </blockquote>
<para>\(f(x) = 3x + 2b\)
  </para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <item> \(f(x) \cdot g(x) =\) _______ </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(9x^2-4b^2\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
  <item> \(f(x) \cdot f(x) = \) _______ </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer: </emphasis>\(9x^2+12xb+4b^2\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="3" type="enumerated">
  <item> \(h(x) \cdot j(x) = \) _______ </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(63x^3-66x^2+4x+8\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="4" type="enumerated">
  <item> \(h(x) \cdot h(x) =\) _______ </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer: </emphasis>\(49x^2+28x+4\)</para></section>
</content>
